<title>USA: Muni survey says material event disclosure up.</title>
<headline>Muni survey says material event disclosure up.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>SEC's secondary market disclosure rule has improved the availability of information from states and local governments about key events affecting their finances, according to over half of those responding to a municipal bond industry survey released Thursday.</p>
<p>PSA The Bond Market Trade Association and National Federation of Municipal Analysts, which conducted the survey, announced the findings at a symposium on the Securities and Exchange Commission's 1994 rule designed to improve secondary market disclosure in the muni market.</p>
</text>
